WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.602
-We're back with my friend
Andy Samberg.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.137
My real-life friend,
it should be stressed.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.437
Hopefully it's clear
to everybody

00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:06.773
that we are good friends.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:09.943
We talk a great deal,
and I've taken to --

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.445
giving you no warning,
I will FaceTime you

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:15.948
while we are filming our segment
we do on YouTube

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:17.917
called "Corrections,"
and I will just call you.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.752
You don't know --
-Right.

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.887
-...you're gonna be on camera
when I answer the phone.

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:24.224
But about half of the time,
you answer.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:27.560
-Yeah, I mean, there's been
a few times when you tried me

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.396
and I was in the bathroom and
I strongly considered answering.

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.432
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.268
-But ultimately,
cooler heads prevailed.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.036
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.204
-You've always --

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.540
-I didn't say what I was doing
in the bathroom.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.209
Maybe I was checking my phone
in the shower.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.710
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.779
-You hate being alone
in the bathroom,

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:48.781
it should be noted,
so I would ima--

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.950
I'm not surprised
you brought your phone.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.285
-Well, thus "Wanna Come With,"

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:55.088
the most classic sketch
ever to be on your show.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.423
-It was weird that you said
"Wanna Come With"

00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:00.760
and that there wasn't just
an explosion of applause.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.328
Do you want to explain
real quick

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.997
the sketch you wrote for "SNL"
called "Wanna Come With"?

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:07.800
-Yeah, it was based
on something I would do

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.635
while we worked at "SNL"

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:12.004
on the writing floor,
on writers' night.

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:13.506
It was a long walk
to the bathroom,

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.842
so I would ask people,
"Wanna come with?"

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.343
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.845
So that I wasn't lonely
on the walk,

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.682
and subsequent, whatever I did
in there, you know?

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.852
-My favorite -- the time
it happened to me,

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.686
which is a story I love telling,

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:30.356
is you'd come into my office
at like 3:00 in the morning

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.025
and you'd say, "Hey, I'm going
to the bathroom,

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.692
wanna come with?"
and I would say,

00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:35.828
"I don't wanna come with,"
and you would close the door.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.430
And I had a frosted glass door,
so you could see the silhouette

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:39.899
of the person outside it.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.335
And you'd be like, "Alright,"
and then you'd close the door

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.003
and you would just stay there.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:47.674
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.675
-And then you'd eventually go,
"I can see you."

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:51.010
and I'd go, "Wanna come with?!"

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.012
-[ Laughs ] "Wanna come with?!"

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.648
This was also -- talk about
hit characters you've done.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:59.151
You came on our show,
and you've left this as a...

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.486
This was a story about --

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:02.689
There was a story, a true story
about mummies.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.190
Some mummies were disturbed.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.527
You came on the show as a mummy
who was upset they got disturbed

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.929
because in -- in the disturbing,

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.597
in the act of being disturbed --

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:13.333
-Yeah.
-...that happened.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.666
-Yeah.

00:02:14.666 --> 00:02:18.505
Okay, well, I can see where
you're going with this,

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:21.840
and it's clickbait,
but fine, okay.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.478
We can cut to a close.
I'll do it. I'll do it.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.280
My doink fell off!

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.615
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.950
That's what everyone wanted,
the catch phrase.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.117
-Yeah. They want it.

00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:33.719
You gave them the catch phrase.

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:35.388
We haven't -- I do --

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.723
Whenever you're on, I do want
to give you the opportunity

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:40.192
to maybe walk back some of the
crueler things you've said

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:42.395
about my dog Frisbee.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.730
You know, I feel like as --

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.531
You know, again,
because you are a parent now,

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:47.534
I feel like you're a more
empathetic person.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.168
You probably know
how hurtful it's been

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:50.703
that you said those things.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.206
-Right, no.
But I will say...

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:54.874
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.543
I do have a little
hot goss to share.

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:59.212
